@kwonoj @Austaras might be related but I found one issue (I can report a new issue as well) where the `arguments` object is not getting the correct reference. Here's a snippet that reproduces it:
```
export class Quirk {
  async doStuff() {
    const args = arguments;
    console.log(args);
    return { foo: null, ...args[0] };
  }
}
```

I have a reproduction here https://github.com/egilsster/swc-jest-issue/blob/main/src/args.test.ts

This starts to work with target set to `es2018`
